      "rationale": "The report says sqlparse's reindent formatter now raises AttributeError('NoneType' object has no attribute 'is_group') for the 'as in parentheses indents' behaviour, which occurs in ReindentFilter._process_parenthesis/_flatten_up_to_token when an AS keyword sits next to a parenthesized sub-query (CTE definitions and derived-table aliases are the canonical real-world examples). The tests assert the documented, always-intended invariants of sqlparse.format(reindent=True) \u2014 it must not crash on valid SQL, must preserve every token of the input, and must place a sub-query's body on its own, further-indented line (the same indentation contract already implemented for plain \"FROM (SELECT ...)\" via the is_dml_dll branch in _process_parenthesis) \u2014 so the expectations come from the formatter's existing, working logic and stated purpose rather than from the current crashing output.",
